{
  "description": "Truncated SHA-256 (first 12 hex chars) of each raw RSNA PatientID confirmed to overlap with BHSD training volumes. This is the public-release redaction of code/data/bhsd_rsna_overlap_patient_ids.json, which contains the raw (unhashed) RSNA PatientIDs and is intentionally excluded from this repository (see .gitignore) because RSNA 2019 is a restricted-use dataset (Kaggle competition rules) and publishing raw PatientID values is a likely data-use-agreement violation. Row order, hash method, and values are identical to Supplementary Table S2 of the companion manuscript (Manuscript_G1_SCI_Full, Section 4.4); data/Supplementary_Table_S2_RSNA_BHSD_Overlap_Hashed.csv in this directory is that same table, copied in for convenience.",
  "date_derived": "2026-09-11T07:11:31.617644+00:00",
  "method": "1) Enumerated all BHSD label_192/images/*.nii.gz filenames (pattern <patient_token>_<study_token>.nii.gz). 2) Read PatientID and StudyInstanceUID DICOM tags directly (pydicom, stop_before_pixels=True) from every file in RSNA stage_2_train/ (no CSV shortcut -- stage_2_train.csv has no PatientID column). 3) Set-intersected BHSD's first filename token against the RSNA PatientID set. 4) For every matched patient, additionally checked whether the BHSD filename's second token appears among the StudyInstanceUID values observed for that RSNA PatientID (compound patient+study identifier confirmation, not a hash/token collision check).",
